# CANONICAL §7.3 fixture — Chamfer `referenceFaces` (kernel-hardening WP-F, 2026-09-03):
# the face an asymmetric chamfer measures `radius` on is a PERSISTED typed ref, not
# "the adjacent face with the smaller snapshot-scoped ordinal".
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS (the defect was measured red-first on `e781272` by
# worker/tests/test_chamfer_reference_face.cpp on ITS OWN box and edge; the
# ordinals below were measured directly on THIS model, 2026-09-03, OCCT 8.0.1): a
# Ø6 hole in the -Y end wall reorders `TopExp::MapShapes` — the +Z top face and the
# -X wall swap ordinal order — so the legacy rule moves the 4 mm leg from the wall
# to the top with the removed volume (80 mm³), the face count and every existing
# check identical. Which PHYSICAL face carries the 4 mm leg is a number, and numbers are
# pinned in ctest (the house split); what this file pins is the PROTOCOL a Rust or
# frontend reader branches on.
#
# THE BOX. Sketch (0,0)-(40,0)-(40,20)-(0,20) on the XY frame (sketch u → world +Y,
# v → world -X), extruded 10: world x ∈ [-20, 0], y ∈ [0, 40], z ∈ [0, 10]. Face
# ordinals on the plain box, measured 2026-09-03 (OCCT 8.0.1): f:1 +X wall, f:2 +Y
# end wall, f:3 -X wall, f:4 -Y end wall, f:5 bottom, f:6 top. The chamfered edge is
# e:10 — top ∩ -X wall, centre (-20, 20, 10) — whose adjacent faces are f:3 and f:6;
# the legacy rule therefore measured `radius` on the -X WALL. e:12 is top ∩ -Y end
# wall (centre (-10, 0, 10)); it meets e:10 at a 90° corner, so the two are two
# CONTOURS. After the -Y end-wall hole (round D) the order is f:5 top < f:6 -X wall
# and the same edge is e:13: exactly the reorder that mirrored the legs.
#
# EVERY REFUSED ROUND RUNS AGAINST THE SAME HEAD (`DiscardPrepared` after each), and
# `GetWorkerHead` re-asserts the head after the refusals. `preparedSnapshotId`
# climbs across discarded rounds (a monotonic scratch counter — see
# chamfer_angle_distance.ndjson), which is why the accepted round D lands on
# snapshot 5, not 2.
#
# NOT pinned here, pinned in ctest: the geometry of every round; `IsSame`
# de-duplication of `adjacentFaces` on a cylinder seam edge (a box has none);
# `CHAMFER_REFERENCE_FACE_CONFLICT` (needs two pairs on one TANGENT chain); the
# descriptor rung for a face ref (every face ref here is a bound id, so it binds on
# the identity rung — the evidence MUST is an authoring rule, §7.3).
